    "love-is-love": {
      "title": "Love is Love",
      "description": "Love doesn’t ask permission to exist. Love is love.",
      "paragraphs": [
        "<p>LOVE IS LOVE is an album for every heart that has ever been told its love was wrong.</p>",
        "<p>These songs ask one simple question: If love is honest, loyal, compassionate, and built to last, why should it be judged by who is holding hands?</p>",
        "<p>Love that protects, forgives, remains faithful, and creates a home does not become less real—or less sacred—because someone else refuses to understand it.</p>",
        "<p>This album isn’t asking for permission or approval. It is refusing to let judgment speak louder than truth. Love is not a label, a political argument, or a rule written by people who have never lived your story.</p>",
        "<p>“They call it rebellion when you love who you want.”</p>",
        "<p>Maybe the greatest rebellion is choosing love anyway.</p>",
        "<p>Love doesn’t ask permission to exist. Love is love.</p>"
      ],
