    "youre-not-god": {
      "title": "You're Not God",
      "description": "You can have your beliefs. You do not get to play God.",
      "paragraphs": [
        "<p>YOU’RE NOT GOD is for everyone who has been judged, shamed, controlled, or cast aside by people claiming they speak for heaven.</p>",
        "<p>This album is not an attack on faith. It is a confrontation with hypocrisy—the preacher demanding purity while hiding their own sins, the believer using scripture as a weapon, and anyone who mistakes personal hatred for God’s voice.</p>",
        "<p>From That Ain’t Holy to Hey Preacher Man, these songs expose what happens when love is replaced by fear, compassion becomes control, and religion is used to excuse cruelty.</p>",
        "<p>No human gets to decide whose life has value, whose love is real, or who deserves grace. You can stand behind a pulpit, a title, or a crowd—but you are still human.</p>",
        "<p>If your faith requires cruelty, that ain’t holy.<br/>If your God sounds exactly like your hate, maybe that’s your voice.</p>",
        "<p>You can have your beliefs. You do not get to play God.</p>",
        "<p>This is YOU’RE NOT GOD.</p>"
      ],
